---
/**
 * ITAD operators segment page (marketing-site story 3; CONTEXT §2 buyer 1).
 */
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Capability from "../../components/Capability.astro";
import { body, grid, h1, h2, h3, item, prose, secondaryLink, section } from "../../lib/ui";
---

<Base
  title="For ITAD operators"
  description="How Wipestation is designed for IT asset disposition operators: fair licensing, proof your customers can check, and your ERP as the system of record."
>
  <h1 class={h1}>For ITAD operators</h1>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>
      You process thousands of assets a week and sell proof of sanitization to your own
      customers. You should not pay for a job that failed, budget extra licences for re-runs, or
      ask your customers to trust a lookup on someone else's server.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class={section} aria-labelledby="fit">
    <h2 id="fit" class={h2}>What it is designed to give you</h2>
    <ul class={grid}>
      <Capability id="per-success-licensing" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>Pay for successes only</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Per-success licensing, designed so a credit is spent only on a verified Clear or Purge
          success, and failures, aborts and re-runs are free.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="outcome-bearing-job" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>One certificate per asset</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed so every attempt on an asset, retries included, composes into one signed
          certificate, so the audit story is never spread across records.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="erp-integration" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>Your ERP stays in charge</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed for REST in and out and webhooks on job changes, with work order identifiers shared so
          reconciliation is a join, not an export.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="fleet-coordination" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>Benches that find each other</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed so stations on one LAN discover each other by mDNS and elect a lead by
          deterministic lead election, with no server to run.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="offline-verification" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>Proof your customer can check</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Offline-verifiable certificates, designed so your customer checks one with the public
          key, without contacting the vendor or you.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="verification-portal" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>A verification portal for your customers</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          A planned branded link you hand your customer, an index over certificates that stay
          checkable on their own.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="r2v3-alignment" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>Records for your R2v3 audit</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed so the method chosen, the outcome and the evidence behind it are on every
          record an R2v3 auditor samples.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="destruction-attestation" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>The destroy path in the same record</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed so that when an asset is physically destroyed, the operator's attestation joins
          its chain of custody.
        </p>
      </Capability>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <p class="mt-10 max-w-prose text-slate-700">
    Want to see it on simulated drives first?
    <a href="/early-access/" class={secondaryLink}>Join early access</a>
  </p>
</Base>
